# ---------------------------------------------------------------- build ----
rust/target/
third_party/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ------------------------------------------------------------ reference ----
# Reference material read while writing this engine, cloned separately and
# not part of what meteor-cfd distributes. See NOTICE. The exceptions are the
# answer keys ofgpu-validate is held against and their manifest: small, tracked.
reference/*
!reference/PROVENANCE.md
!reference/ghia1982/
!reference/ho-powell-liley1972/
!reference/kadoya1985/
!reference/nasa-glenn2002/
!reference/mcbride-gordon-reno1993/
!reference/ivptestset2008/
!reference/tnf-flameD/
!reference/martin_moyce_1952/
!reference/riboux_gordillo_2014/
!reference/rae2822/
# docs/17 VAL-01 (decision D-VAL-1): the two SPEC-LIT 110.3 / 110.4
# transcriptions are US Government data and are tracked. The MKM channel DNS
# profiles are NOT: their host states no terms, so reference/mkm99/ stays
# ignored by reference/* above and tools/keys/fetch_answer_keys.py fetches it.
!reference/driver_seegmiller_1985/
!reference/mccaffrey_1979/
# docs/17 VAL-04 (decision D-VAL-2): the ERCOFTAC T3A summary table is CC BY-NC-SA,
# so reference/ercoftac_t3a/ stays ignored by reference/* and is fetched (SPEC-LIT 144.1).
# docs/17 DST-00: the dust stream's answer keys (SPEC-LIT 151.6), digitised from the
# two open Huang et al. papers and H22's Table 1 as printed; small and tracked.
!reference/huang2020-leeds/
!reference/huang2022-rembe/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- cases ----
# Every case here is GENERATED by `ofgpu-generate-mesh`, and the meshes and
# results run to hundreds of megabytes. Regenerate rather than clone:
#
#   cargo run --release --bin ofgpu-generate-mesh -- channel  ../cases/channel  200 120 1
#   cargo run --release --bin ofgpu-generate-mesh -- cavity   ../cases/cavity    80  80 1
#   cargo run --release --bin ofgpu-generate-mesh -- damBreak ../cases/damBreak  60 100 1
#
# ...but the .jsonc case DEFINITIONS are the opposite of generated data: a
# few kB of text each, referenced by docs/07-lowmach-solver.md and by
# ofgpu-validate, and without them a fresh clone can reproduce nothing.
cases/*
!cases/README.md
!cases/*.jsonc
# docs/17 DST-07/08: the dust gates' case definitions (SPEC-LIT 157.5,
# 157.6) live in one folder; only their .jsonc files are tracked.
!cases/dust/
cases/dust/*
!cases/dust/*.jsonc
# docs/17 CHR-02b: the mechanism folder's README (SPEC-LIT 129.6). Only the
# README is tracked: GRI-Mech 3.0 and DRM19 have no redistribution grant, so a
# copy a user downloads into this folder must stay untracked.
!cases/mech/
cases/mech/*
!cases/mech/README.md
# The race-car sample is a geometry and a recipe, not a mesh: 52 kB of STL and
# the two commands that turn it into a 2.1-million-cell run. The mesh and the
# results it produces are a gigabyte, and they are what the user's own machine
# is for.
!cases/racecar.stl
!cases/racecar.md
!cases/racecar.cmd
# The pressure and temperature the momentum solver needs and the mesher does not
# write. Uniform fields: the boundary conditions are the whole content, so this
# is 2 kB, not the 40 MB a solved p and T are.
!cases/racecar.fields/
# SPEC-LIT 110.3 Gate 110-B: the closed box the step is carved out of, and the
# recipe that runs the castellated mesh end to end. 86 lines of ASCII.
!cases/backstep.stl
!cases/backstep.cmd
# Retired case definitions - kept as dated records of measurements that were
# taken before a later SPEC-LIT rule made the cases themselves unrunnable.
# They are records, not cases; cases/retired/README.md says what replaced each.
!cases/retired/
# Turek-Hron FSI benchmark: the two case skeletons are text; the meshes that
# tools/mesh/examples/turek_hron.py writes beside them are regenerated, not kept.
!cases/turekHron/
cases/turekHron/mesh/
cases/turekHron/mesh_L*/

# ------------------------------------------------------------- results -----
*.png
*.mp4

# ------------------------------------------------------------ packaging ----
# Built installers. `packaging/iterations.iss` is the recipe; the output is not
# part of the source tree - it belongs to a GitHub release.
/dist/
